WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.988
A planning commission does two different jobs, and mixing them up is how good intentions become bad votes.

2
00:00:05.988 --> 00:00:07.231
One job writes policy.

3
00:00:07.231 --> 00:00:09.998
The other applies policy that is already written.

4
00:00:09.998 --> 00:00:17.229
Torrance's commission has seven members, appointed by the City Council, and most nights the second job is the one on the agenda.

5
00:00:17.229 --> 00:00:25.659
The power underneath both jobs is the police power: the city's authority to regulate land for the public health, safety, and welfare.

6
00:00:25.659 --> 00:00:27.561
Zoning grew out of that power.

7
00:00:27.561 --> 00:00:31.364
Los Angeles adopted an early industrial restriction in 1909.

8
00:00:31.364 --> 00:00:35.547
New York adopted the first comprehensive zoning ordinance in 1916.

9
00:00:35.547 --> 00:00:40.491
The United States Supreme Court upheld zoning in Euclid versus Ambler in 1926.

10
00:00:40.491 --> 00:00:45.372
California required cities and counties to adopt a master plan the next year.

11
00:00:45.372 --> 00:00:52.661
Since then California has rewritten planning law faster than almost any other state, mostly because it grew faster.

12
00:00:52.661 --> 00:00:59.986
When the commission recommends a general plan amendment, a zoning change, or a specific plan, it is doing legislative work.

13
00:00:59.986 --> 00:01:03.439
It is helping the council decide what the rules should be.

14
00:01:03.439 --> 00:01:10.407
That is the moment for vision, for tradeoffs, and for a public argument about what kind of city Torrance ought to be.

15
00:01:10.407 --> 00:01:11.955
The commission recommends.

16
00:01:11.955 --> 00:01:13.087
The council adopts.

17
00:01:13.087 --> 00:01:21.662
When the commission decides a conditional use permit, a design review, a subdivision, or a similar entitlement, it is doing quasi-judicial work.

18
00:01:21.662 --> 00:01:23.091
The rules already exist.

19
00:01:23.091 --> 00:01:30.594
The hearing is not the place to renegotiate the density the council adopted, or to substitute one person's taste for the code.

20
00:01:30.594 --> 00:01:36.430
The job is to measure the project against the adopted standards, take evidence, and make findings.

21
00:01:36.430 --> 00:01:39.371
Four legal habits protect either kind of decision.

22
00:01:39.371 --> 00:01:41.606
Meet in the open, under the Brown Act.

23
00:01:41.606 --> 00:01:47.017
Give every party a fair hearing: the applicant, the neighbor, and anyone who wrote a letter.

24
00:01:47.017 --> 00:01:52.016
Notice the hearing the way the code requires, because a bad notice is a bad decision.

25
00:01:52.016 --> 00:01:55.780
And follow the state laws that now sit on top of the local code.

26
00:01:55.780 --> 00:01:58.603
Personal preference is not one of the standards.

27
00:01:58.603 --> 00:02:00.897
A clean motion does three small things.

28
00:02:00.897 --> 00:02:03.368
It says what you are approving or denying.

29
00:02:03.368 --> 00:02:06.838
It ties that action to the findings the ordinance requires.

30
00:02:06.838 --> 00:02:10.955
And it adopts the environmental determination first, then the project.

31
00:02:10.955 --> 00:02:17.307
If you need a continuance, take one because the record is incomplete, not because the room is uncomfortable.

32
00:02:17.307 --> 00:02:27.835
On a housing project that already meets objective standards, continuances and appeals count toward a five-hearing cap, so a delay is a legal event, not just a scheduling courtesy.

33
00:02:27.835 --> 00:02:34.305
The record you build is the lawsuit, if there is one, and it is also the story the next commissioner inherits.

34
00:02:34.305 --> 00:02:38.657
Housing, private investment, and public trust all run through that record.

35
00:02:38.657 --> 00:02:42.539
Predictable process is what makes the next honest project show up.

36
00:02:42.539 --> 00:02:52.361
For the legal framework, see the 2026 Cal Cities Planning Commissioners Academy session Planning Commission 101, and confirm Torrance procedure with the city attorney.
